  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategy for Strengthening the Social Fabric of Victims Communities in Colombia, in the Process of Return, Relocation and Local Integration &#x201c;TEJI&#xc9;NDONOS&#x201d; in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to contribute to the Colombian Government&apos;s efforts towards strengthening the social fabric and generating bonds of trust between the communities that have been victims of forced displacement and the receiving communities, within the framework of the return, relocation, and local integration processes, through the TEJI&#xc9;NDONOS Strategy. To this end, it is expected that 41 communities of victim population prioritized by the UARIV (by its acronym in Spanish) achieve the re-establishment of trust among them and the social cohesion through the recovery of social/traditional practices and territorial rooting to foster a sense of community and promote dynamics in favor of the alternative resolution of community conflicts. The project will provide tools that allow the communities to participate in decision-making, generating strategies to promote participatory practices and to reverse the differential effects and conflicts impacts on the communities based on a differential approach. The project aims to generate this impact in the communities through training. The project will be implemented within the framework of 4 thematic axes: community recognition, construction of a sense of community, conflict management, and public participation.</narrative>
  </description>
